{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.CurvatureRank","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.CurvatureRank","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.curvatureRank_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.curvatureRank_le","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank.lean#L37-L43","doc":"If `r₀` witnesses the curvature-rank condition, the curvature-rank\nis `≤ r₀` (the infimum is bounded by any witness). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.curvatureRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.curvatureRank","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank.lean#L27-L35","doc":"The **curvature-rank** of `x`, given a GB-filtration grade\n`grade : A → ℕ` on the iterated-curvature images: it is the least\n`r` such that `gradeOfIter x r = r`, i.e. the iterated curvature\n`F^r x` first occupies filtration step `r`. We package the\n\"first non-trivial step\" content as the least element of the set of\nwitnessing indices. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:curvature-rank","label":"def:curvature-rank","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}